DerbyNet on Raspberry Pi
========================

The guide is docs/raspberry-pi.md (at the top of this repository, or on
GitHub: https://github.com/redshedjed/derbynet/blob/master/docs/raspberry-pi.md).

What's here:

  setup.sh          turns a fresh Raspberry Pi OS install into a DerbyNet Pi:
                      bash installer/rpi/setup.sh --roles "server timer"
  derbynet-pi       installed as /usr/local/bin/derbynet-pi; manages the roles
                    (derbynet-pi status, doctor, apply, promote, ...)
  derbynet-pi.conf  the settings file, installed as derbynet.conf on the SD
                    card's boot partition; it explains every setting
  kiosk.sh          the full-screen kiosk browser, started by
                    "derbynet-pi desktop" at desktop login
